---
description: Core rules for the Promptstack School Management System
alwaysApply: true
---

You are building a production-grade School Management System for a Cameroonian school, delivered by Promptstack Technologies.

NON-NEGOTIABLES
- Language: TypeScript (strict mode) everywhere. No `any` unless justified in a comment.
- The system runs LOCALLY on one Windows 10/11 PC (the "school server") and is used by other PCs on the same LAN through a browser. It MUST work with NO internet connection.
- Money is stored as INTEGER FCFA (XAF has no decimals). Never use floats for money.
- Payments, receipts and audit logs are APPEND-ONLY. Never hard-delete or silently edit a payment. Corrections = reversal or adjustment entry with a reason, linked to the original, with audit trail.
- Every write action records who, when, what changed (before/after) in the audit log.
- All permissions are enforced on the SERVER. Hiding a button in the UI is never enough.
- Validate all input on the server with Zod. Return consistent error shapes.
- Every feature ships with tests (unit for business rules, integration for API, e2e for critical flows).
- No placeholder code, no TODO stubs, no fake data in production paths. Seed data lives only in the seed script.
- Small, focused commits. After each task: run typecheck, lint, tests. Fix failures before moving on.
- UI: purple and white design system (see tokens in docs/SPEC.md section 11). Accessible, keyboard friendly, responsive down to 1024px wide, printable reports.
- When a requirement is ambiguous, choose the safest sensible default, document it in docs/DECISIONS.md, and continue. Do not stop to ask unless it blocks progress.
